# AirMouse: downward optical flow + downward rangefinder, fused by EKF3 as horizontal VELOCITY.
# SLAM (ExtNav) still gives position and yaw; flow gives a second, independent velocity measurement, so the
# EKF does not integrate accelerometer error when SLAM updates are late or jump (IMU drift between fixes).
# Flow alone does NOT fix a SLAM map that has slipped a cell - the EKF follows SLAM's position.
#
# Sim: ArduPilot SITL simulates both sensors from its own physics state (flat floor), no Gazebo sensor needed.
# Real drone: set FLOW_TYPE to the real sensor (e.g. 6 = MSP/MTF-01, 5 = MAVLink, 1 = PX4Flow/PMW3901 via I2C
# depends on the board) and RNGFND1_TYPE to its range sensor, then calibrate FLOW_FXSCALER/FYSCALER.

# optical flow: 10 = SITL
FLOW_TYPE 10
SIM_FLOW_ENABLE 1
# flow needs height above the floor: downward rangefinder (gazebo-iris.parm already sets RNGFND1_TYPE 1,
# the SITL sonar); make sure it points down and covers indoor heights
RNGFND1_ORIENT 25
RNGFND1_MIN 0.05
RNGFND1_MAX 8.00

# EKF3 source set 1: position + yaw from SLAM (ExtNav, nogps_extnav.parm), horizontal velocity from flow (5)
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 5
